From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 11:04:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Keep savegames with the game settings

Savegames go directly in the config directory. The DS startup selects
a separate directory for each game or mod, keeping their slots apart.
---
 doomgeneric/m_config.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/doomgeneric/m_config.c b/doomgeneric/m_config.c
index 865e168..fb7c59d 100644
--- a/doomgeneric/m_config.c
+++ b/doomgeneric/m_config.c
@@ -2115,7 +2115,7 @@ char *M_GetSaveGameDir(char *iwadname)
 
         free(topdir);
 #else
-        savegamedir = M_StringJoin(configdir, DIR_SEPARATOR_S, ".savegame/", NULL);
+        savegamedir = M_StringJoin(configdir, DIR_SEPARATOR_S, NULL);
 
         M_MakeDirectory(savegamedir);
 
